D2DX 0.99.529: show the HRESULT that was passed in the message of ComException.

The constructor built the message from the member hr before it was set,
so every fatal error reported HRESULT 0x00000000. The app ships the
prebuilt glide3x.dll of the D2DX 0.99.529 release with a three-byte change,
applied by tools/binpatch.py (patch "d2dx-glide3x") when the assets are
fetched:

  file      glide3x.dll
  before    sha256 06cc9e9b49902f1ef3aa28180a9859327df717d9022fb1774eeda6f0ba0546d8
  after     sha256 5c4997371d9ca183bd7f0b17bc2f33eb9193f85e34cd94cc7153127b68bc5725
  change    file offset 0x10fd4: 8b 4b 0c -> 8b 4d 08 (mov ecx, [ebx+0xc] -> mov ecx, [ebp+8])

The source change it corresponds to:

--- a/src/d2dx/ErrorHandling.h
+++ b/src/d2dx/ErrorHandling.h
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 	struct ComException final : public std::runtime_error
 	{
 		ComException(HRESULT hr_, const char* func_, int32_t line_) :
-			std::runtime_error(detail::GetMessageForHRESULT(hr, func_, line_)),
+			std::runtime_error(detail::GetMessageForHRESULT(hr_, func_, line_)),
 			hr{ hr_ },
 			func{ func_ },
 			line{ line_ }
